  "status": "ANNOTATION ONLY -- the paper log is NOT rewritten, re-scored or adjusted (standing directive s.13; the Integrity Gate holds the veto). This file is the caveat the record now carries.",
  "the_defect": {
    "series": "VXN (data/VXNCLS_MAX.csv), coverage end 2026-09-02",
    "consumer": "src/risk_state_engine.py:decision_for -> market_state_primitives_v2.extend_state_frame (vxn_level_vs_trailing)",
    "mechanism": "extend_state_frame reindexed the VXN daily series with method='ffill', which is correct for a holiday INSIDE the series and wrong past its end. Every session after 2026-09-02 was handed the 2026-09-02 close (21.07) as though it were that day's volatility reading. B2 turned that number into vxn_high (>= the frozen HIGH-tercile edge 0.02545542283434844), and vxn_high sets expected_range_mult, stop_distance_atr, target_distance_atr, size_multiplier and can set trade_permission.",
    "second_defect": "src/risk_state_engine.py:_event_days() read research/calendars/event_days.csv, which has never existed on disk, so is_event_day was False for EVERY session B2 has ever scored and the directive's scheduled-event trade_permission veto silently never fired. The FOMC/CPI/NFP calendar (coverage end 2021-09-22) could not have answered for a 2026 session either.",
    "why_it_matters": "The live paper record starts 2026-09-08, which is AFTER the VXN coverage end. There is no session in the paper log that was scored on a measured VXN value."
  },
