    "vxn_high_flag_on_every_session": false,
    "consequence": "vxn_factor stayed 1.0 on every live session, so expected_range_mult was the base (prior-day / overnight) product alone and size_multiplier came from that. The flag being False is NOT a finding -- it is what the invented input happened to produce. To flip it the true reading needed rel >= +0.0255, i.e. a VXN close of roughly 21.9 or above, a level this same series printed on 2026-09-01 (21.96). Whether any of these six sessions was truly a HIGH-tercile session is UNKNOWN and stays unknown until data/VXNCLS_MAX.csv is extended.",
